<title>UK: Sainsbury says happy with Giant.</title>
<headline>Sainsbury says happy with Giant.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British supermarket operator J. Sainsbury Plc rejected a report in Monday's Evening Standard that Ahold NV of the Netherlands was interested in buying the UK firm's stake in U.S. food retailer Giant Food Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;The article is pure speculation and we never comment on rumour and speculation,&quot; a Sainsbury spokeswoman said. &quot;We are happy with our relationship with Giant and have no plans to change that relationship.&quot;</p>
<p>Sainsbury shares were down 1/2p at 426 by 1034 GMT, in modest volume of just under one million shares.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
